A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Faithful and Unfaithful Servant, the Talents and the Pharisee and the Tax Collector are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. Their meanings are not used here, and the meaning of this passage is not used there.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus asks which of the hearers, having a servant who has come in from plowing or feeding cattle, will tell him to sit down to meat, and whether he will not rather tell him to make ready, gird himself and serve until the man has eaten and drunken. He asks whether the man thanks that servant because he did what was commanded, and the short answer is “I trow not.” Then He tells the hearers to say, when they have done all that is commanded them, “We are unprofitable servants: we have done that which was our duty to do.” He names nothing else in the passage.'))
