A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names the hearers, the time, the words to say and the reason given, and nothing more. No identity for the man, the servant, the field, the cattle, the meal or the commands. No symbol carried in from another parable, and the word “unprofitable” in Matthew 25:30 is not read into Luke 17:10. Doing what is commanded and saying “unprofitable” are actions in a story and in a saying, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is not the servant. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))
